 {"name": "The literal sense, read by genre", "who": "Augustine, Aquinas, Calvin; most Catholic, Orthodox and Protestant scholars today", "view": "The literal sense is what the writer meant, so it includes figures and depends on genre; Genesis 1 can be literally true without being a scientific account.", "evidence": "Aquinas on 'God's arm'; Augustine's rules; the many genres of the Bible; Augustine's warning about talking nonsense on nature."},
